+# Paging Links Carry the Active Narrowing, and Only When One Is Active
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-004` narrows the paged veterinarian directory to one specialty. Two of its acceptance criteria pull against each other in the template. Paging must stay inside the narrowed list, so every paging link has to carry the specialty forward. With no specialty asked for, the surface must behave as it did before narrowing existed, so the same links must render exactly as they rendered before.
+
+A single unconditional link form does not satisfy both. Thymeleaf's link-parameter syntax renders a null parameter as an empty one — `@{/vets.html(page=${i}, specialty=${specialty})}` with a null specialty produces `/vets.html?page=2&specialty=` — rather than omitting it. The design for this slice assumed the opposite, and the regression test asserting that unnarrowed paging links carry no specialty is what caught it.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Render the parameter unconditionally** — accept `?specialty=` on unnarrowed URLs. The controller already maps an empty value to "nothing asked for", so the pages served are identical. The URLs are not: every bookmark, shared link, and access-log line for the plain directory changes shape, and the empty parameter is visible to readers who never asked to narrow anything.
+2. **Build the query string in the controller** — hand the template a prebuilt URL per link. It takes URL construction away from the rendering engine that knows the request context and the encoding rules, and adds presentation assembly to a controller that already carries more than the pattern catalog admits.
+3. **Select the link form in the template** — one flag on the paging block records whether a narrowing is active, and each link picks the parameterized URL or the plain one.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. A paged listing that can be narrowed carries the active narrowing in its paging links, and renders the plain URL when nothing is narrowed.
+
+The unnarrowed URL is part of the surface a requirement freezes, not an implementation detail underneath it. A criterion that says a surface behaves as it did before is read to include the addresses it hands out.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Unnarrowed paging URLs stay byte-identical to the ones the directory rendered before narrowing existed, and the guarantee is held by a test rather than by inspection.
+- The paging block is more verbose: each of its links states both forms. A comment in the template records the rendering behavior that forces it, so the verbosity does not read as an accident.
+- The two-form selection does not scale. A listing narrowed by more than one optional parameter would need a form per combination, and extracting a shared paging fragment is the remedy at that point rather than a third ternary.
+- Owner paging does not follow this rule and drops its search term entirely, which widens a name search to every owner from the second page on. That is recorded under [Known Defects](../system-design.md#known-defects); this decision sets the rule for narrowable listings from here on and does not retrofit it.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-004
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md: Presentation](../system-design.md#presentation)
+- [ADR: Server-Side HTML Rendering with Thymeleaf](2026-07-31-server-side-rendering-with-thymeleaf.md)
